  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BRITISH COLUMBIA: CIJV &amp; PBHJV WETLAND-A</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funds under this award are to be used to benefit 48,402 acres of migratory bird habitat in the province of British Columbia, including focus areas located in Elk/Flathead, Rocky Mountain Trench, South Selkirks, South Okanagan, West Chilcotin, Central Coast, Salish Sea and Central Coast Rainforest Natural Areas. This project will prevent degradation and fragmentation of waterfowl habitats, and will provide increased foraging and breeding opportunities for a variety of wetland-dependent migratory birds, including American Widgeon, Barrow&apos;s Goldeneye, Redhead, Wood Duck, and Ringed-necked Duck.</narrative>
  </description>
